GOAL
Add a new render-layer screen `WhoAreYouUI` (src/render/whoareyou.ts) shown on the player's FIRST Play — i.e. when no character has been chosen yet (localStorage 'rs_selected_character' is unset). It lets the new player choose a male or female Explorer appearance, records it, and proceeds into the normal flow. On every subsequent Play it is skipped.

HARD RULES (state and obey):
- NEVER edit game/test/** or game/accept/** (tamper guard reverts+blocks). 
- This is a src/render/** screen: performance.now is allowed for animation; do NOT import from src/sim/** except pure data (you may import from src/sim/data/characters if convenient, but it is not required). Do NOT put any game logic in sim.
- Keep the gate green (`npm run -s typecheck` + tests). Run them.
- Game must never break on missing art: getTexture(key) returns a grey-box placeholder synchronously and swaps in real art async. A Sprite must reassign `.texture = getTexture(key)` every frame in sync() to adopt real art once it loads (mirror how charselect.ts refreshes its background/char sprites).

PRE-FACT (verified): texture keys panel.whoareyou, player.explorer_m, player.explorer_f are NOT yet in game/assets/manifest.json. That is fine — getTexture auto-declares unknown keys as placeholders. Reference them by key; do not edit the manifest, do not block on them.

STEP 1 — CREATE src/render/whoareyou.ts
Model the class after CharSelectUI / SettingsUI structure (constructor builds a `readonly root = new Container()`; `init(app, onDone)`; `show()`; `hide()`; `sync(screenW, screenH)`; a keydown handler installed in init and gated on `this.root.visible`). Specifics:
- Background: a Sprite whose texture is refreshed each frame to getTexture('panel.whoareyou'); stretch to screenW x screenH (anchor 0). Add a translucent dark overlay Graphics on top for legibility (match charselect's 0x070714 @ ~0.5 alpha pattern).
- Title Text near top, centered: 'WHO ARE YOU?' (monospace, gold #f5d76e, bold, ~28px, matching charselect title style).
- Two large choice tiles side by side, centered vertically: LEFT = Male Explorer, RIGHT = Female Explorer. Each tile = a Container holding: a Sprite (texture refreshed each frame to getTexture('player.explorer_m') for male, getTexture('player.explorer_f') for female; scale ~2.6 like charselect), a caption Text below it ('MALE' / 'FEMALE', or 'EXPLORER (M)' / 'EXPLORER (F)'), and a subtle framed background Graphics. Make each tile interactive (interactive=true, cursor='pointer') with pointerover/pointerout hover feedback (scale bump or tint) mirroring charselect.
- Selection on click: define `_choose(gender: 'male'|'female')` that:
    localStorage.setItem('rs_explorer_gender', gender);
    localStorage.setItem('rs_selected_character', 'explorer');
    // ensure the unlock set exists with explorer
    if (!localStorage.getItem('rs_unlocked_characters')) localStorage.setItem('rs_unlocked_characters', JSON.stringify(['explorer']));
    this.hide();
    if (this._onDone) this._onDone();
  IMPORTANT: call this.hide() BEFORE invoking the onDone callback (this mirrors the CharSelect §AUDIT-2026-07-02 CRIT-8 fix — leaving root.visible true would block the next screen's sim-step/render and can soft-lock the flow).
- Keyboard: ArrowLeft/ArrowRight moves a highlight between the two tiles; Enter confirms the highlighted one via _choose; default highlight = male (left). Draw the highlight as a gold stroke around the active tile (mirror charselect _applyHighlights).
- sync(screenW, screenH): reposition/scale background, overlay, title, and the two tiles responsively (center the pair with a horizontal spread like charselect's hSpread). Return early if `!this.root.visible`.
- Remove the keydown listener is not required (charselect keeps its listener installed and gates on visibility — do the same).

STEP 2 — WIRE INTO main.ts (boot/Play flow)
Current flow: MainMenu Play callback does `mainMenu.root.visible=false; charSelect.show();`. Also the mainMenu.init Play callback and the top-of-file construction happen in main(). Change so the FIRST play routes through WhoAreYou:
- Construct `const whoAreYou = new WhoAreYouUI();` alongside the other UIs.
- `whoAreYou.init(renderer.app, () => { charSelect.show(); });` — after the player picks a gender, proceed to the character-select screen (which will now default-select Explorer). (Do NOT jump straight to worldmap; the GDD says choose gender THEN continue to selection/start.)
- Add `whoAreYou.sync(W, H);` to the ticker sync block alongside the other `*.sync(W,H)` calls.
- Gate the main-loop sim-step/render guards so they also treat whoAreYou as an overlay screen: the big `if (!outcomeShown && !worldMap.root.visible && !mainMenu.root.visible && !charSelect.root.visible && !settingsUI.visible)` and the `renderer.sync` guard `if (!worldMap.root.visible && !mainMenu.root.visible && !charSelect.root.visible)` must also include `&& !whoAreYou.root.visible` so the sim doesn't step and the stage doesn't render while this screen is up.
- Change the MainMenu Play callback to branch on first-play:
    mainMenu.init(renderer.app, () => {
      mainMenu.root.visible = false;
      if (!localStorage.getItem('rs_selected_character')) {
        whoAreYou.show();      // first-ever play -> choose your Explorer
      } else {
        charSelect.show();     // returning player -> straight to character select
      }
    }, () => { /* settings, unchanged */ });
- Make sure whoAreYou is hidden at boot (its init sets root.visible=false; also ensure setStageVisible(false) path is unaffected).

ACCEPTANCE (must be objectively verifiable):
1. Gate: `npm run -s typecheck` exits 0 and tests pass. Report the commands and that they were green.
2. First-play path: run the app with a CLEARED localStorage (via preview_eval `localStorage.clear()` then reload, OR fresh profile). From Main Menu, click Play. A snapshot/accessibility-snapshot shows the 'WHO ARE YOU?' screen with a Male and a Female Explorer choice (grey-box placeholders acceptable). Confirm the sim is NOT running behind it (stage children hidden / renderer.sync skipped).
3. Choice persists: click the Female tile (or Arrow+Enter). Verify via preview_eval: `localStorage.getItem('rs_explorer_gender') === 'female'` and `localStorage.getItem('rs_selected_character') === 'explorer'` and `JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('rs_unlocked_characters')).includes('explorer')`. After the pick, the Character-Select screen is shown (snapshot shows EXPLORER/WARRIOR/ROGUE roster) and the WhoAreYou root is hidden (`whoAreYou.root.visible === false`).
4. Returning-player path: with 'rs_selected_character' already set, click Play from Main Menu — the WhoAreYou screen is SKIPPED and Character Select shows directly (snapshot proof).
5. No soft-lock: after choosing a gender and proceeding, you can reach the world map and start a run normally (the hide-before-onDone ordering prevents the overlay from blocking sim-step).

GOAL
Add party assembly to the character-select screen: the player picks ONE Leader plus up to TWO Supports from the UNLOCKED characters, forming a party of up to 3. Persist the party. At run start, every in-party character contributes its weaponPool to the level-up draft pool, and every in-party character's passive is applied — all inside the DETERMINISTIC sim (pure). Meta-mechanics may be stubbed with a clear TODO. Warn the player if they start with fewer than 3 party members.

DEPENDENCIES: this spec builds on char_roster_gdd.txt (which creates src/sim/data/characters.ts with CHARACTERS/CharacterId/CharacterDef/PassiveTraining and rewires charselect + startRun to the registry). Assume that spec has landed. If characters.ts does not yet exist, STOP and report — do not recreate it.

HARD RULES (state and obey):
- NEVER edit game/test/** or game/accept/** (tamper guard reverts+blocks).
- src/sim/** MUST stay deterministic: NO Math.random, Date.now, performance.now, requestAnimationFrame. Passive application and pool contribution live in sim as PURE functions of (party, character defs, player/state) — they must produce identical results for the same inputs. Use only s.rng for any randomness (there should be none needed for applying passives).
- src/render/** MAY use performance.now for animation.
- Keep the gate green (`npm run -s typecheck` + tests). Run them.
- Never break on missing art. getTexture returns a placeholder synchronously; refresh sprite .texture each frame in sync().

PRE-FACT (verified): texture keys panel.party, icon.leader, icon.support are NOT yet in game/assets/manifest.json. Fine — getTexture auto-declares them as placeholders. Reference by key; do not edit the manifest.

DATA MODEL (localStorage):
- 'rs_party' = JSON `{ leader: CharacterId, supports: CharacterId[] }` (supports length 0..2, never includes the leader, no duplicates). If absent/invalid, derive a default at read time: `{ leader: (rs_selected_character || 'explorer'), supports: [] }`. Keep 'rs_selected_character' in sync with `rs_party.leader` (the leader IS the character you play as; the existing startRun loadout keys off rs_selected_character).

STEP 1 — PURE SIM HELPERS in src/sim/data/characters.ts
Add (do not remove existing exports):

  export interface PartySelection { leader: CharacterId; supports: CharacterId[]; }

  // The full set of in-party members (leader first, then supports), deduped, order-stable.
  export function partyMembers(p: PartySelection): CharacterId[] {
    const out: CharacterId[] = [p.leader];
    for (const s of p.supports) if (s !== p.leader && !out.includes(s)) out.push(s);
    return out;
  }

  // Union of every in-party character's weaponPool, deduped, order-stable (leader's pool first).
  export function partyWeaponPool(p: PartySelection): string[] {
    const out: string[] = [];
    for (const id of partyMembers(p)) for (const w of CHARACTERS[id].weaponPool) if (!out.includes(w)) out.push(w);
    return out;
  }

  // Aggregate passive multipliers/additions to apply to a fresh player at run start.
  // Deterministic, pure. Interpret each in-party character's passive by its id:
  //   'determination' -> maxHp *= (1 + perLevel * trainingLevel)   (health)
  //   'weapon_mastery' -> damageMult *= (1 + perLevel * trainingLevel) (damage)
  //   'magnet'        -> magnetMult *= (1 + perLevel * trainingLevel) (pickup range)
  // trainingLevel defaults to 1 (outside-adventure upgrading of training levels is OUT OF SCOPE here; pass 1).
  // Return a plain struct the caller applies; do NOT mutate anything here.
  export interface PartyPassives { hpMult: number; damageMult: number; magnetMult: number; }
  export function partyPassives(p: PartySelection, trainingLevel = 1): PartyPassives { ... }

Implement partyPassives by starting from {hpMult:1, damageMult:1, magnetMult:1} and, for each member, switching on member.passive.id to multiply the matching field by (1 + passive.perLevel * trainingLevel). Unknown passive ids are ignored (no-op). Keep it pure.

STEP 2 — APPLY PARTY AT RUN START (deterministic)
The existing loadout is applied in main.ts startRun() (render/host layer) which sets st.player.weapons/maxHp/hp/speed from the leader's CharacterDef (per char_roster_gdd.txt). Extend the run-start path so party passives + pool are applied deterministically. Two acceptable wiring options — pick ONE and state which:
  (A) SIM-SIDE (preferred, keeps determinism obvious): add an exported pure function in sim, e.g. in src/sim/data/characters.ts or a thin new sim helper, `applyPartyToPlayer(player, party, trainingLevel=1)` that multiplies player.maxHp by hpMult (and sets player.hp = player.maxHp), player.attackDamage by damageMult, player.magnetRadius by magnetMult. Also expose the draft pool as data the upgrade system can read (see STEP 3). Call this from startRun() right after the leader loadout is set. Because it only reads the party + defs and mutates the passed-in player, it is deterministic.
  (B) HOST-SIDE: compute PartyPassives in startRun() via partyPassives(party) and apply the same multiplications inline. Still deterministic since it's pure math over static data.
Either way: read 'rs_party' in startRun() (default {leader: rs_selected_character||'explorer', supports:[]}), and apply. State clearly in a comment that this runs once at run start and uses no wall-clock/random.
NOTE the ordering: leader base stats (maxHp/speed/default weapon) are set first (from char_roster_gdd.txt), THEN party passive multipliers are applied on top. Set player.hp = player.maxHp AFTER the hp multiplier so the player starts at full.

STEP 3 — PARTY WEAPON POOL FEEDS THE LEVEL-UP DRAFT
The level-up draft (src/sim/systems/upgrades.ts buildLevelDraft) currently offers new weapons from the ENTIRE WEAPON_POOL. Constrain/extend it so the 'weapon:new:<id>' candidates come from the PARTY'S weapon pool (partyWeaponPool) rather than every weapon in the game. Implementation guidance (keep it deterministic and minimal — you MAY edit src/sim/systems/upgrades.ts even though it's not in this spec's `files` list; state that you did):
  - Store the resolved party pool on GameState at run start (add a field, e.g. `partyWeaponPool: string[]` to GameState in src/sim/state.ts, default [] in newGame). Populate it in the run-start path (STEP 2). This keeps buildLevelDraft pure (reads state, no localStorage in sim).
  - In buildLevelDraft, when adding `weapon:new:<id>` candidates, if `s.partyWeaponPool.length > 0` restrict the WEAPON_POOL iteration to ids present in s.partyWeaponPool; otherwise fall back to the full WEAPON_POOL (so existing tests/headless runs with no party set are unchanged). Leave the already-equipped default weapon always level-up-able. Do NOT change chest-draft behavior unless trivial.
  - IMPORTANT determinism/test-safety: the fallback (empty partyWeaponPool -> full pool) MUST preserve the exact current candidate ordering and rng draw sequence when no party is set, so existing headless/gate tests stay green. If you cannot guarantee identical sequencing, gate the new behavior behind `s.partyWeaponPool.length > 0` so the no-party path is byte-identical to today. Run the tests and confirm.

STEP 4 — PARTY UI ON CHARACTER SELECT (src/render/charselect.ts)
Add party-assembly UI using panel.party as a side/overlay panel plus icon.leader / icon.support badges:
- Read unlocked set from 'rs_unlocked_characters' (default ['explorer']); only unlocked characters can be added to the party.
- Interaction: the existing per-character SELECT becomes 'Set as Leader'. Add a second action per character 'Add/Remove Support' (a small button or a second tap target). Enforce: exactly one leader; supports max 2; a character cannot be both leader and support (choosing an existing support as leader removes it from supports, and vice-versa); leader defaults to the currently highlighted/selected character.
- Show a party panel (backed by getTexture('panel.party'), ~300x360) listing the current party: the leader row badged with getTexture('icon.leader'), each support row badged with getTexture('icon.support'). Empty support slots shown as '(empty)'.
- Persist to 'rs_party' whenever the party changes, and keep 'rs_selected_character' === rs_party.leader.
- START/CONTINUE button (this can reuse/extend the existing SELECT/confirm button, or add a 'START ADVENTURE' button): on click it persists the party and hands back via the existing onBack callback (which proceeds to the world map). BEFORE handing back, if the party has fewer than 3 members (leader + 2 supports), show a non-blocking warning (a red/amber Text line like 'Starting with an incomplete party (N/3).') — the player may still proceed. Do NOT hard-block. (Mirror the CharSelect hide-before-onBack ordering to avoid the soft-lock.)
- Keep all sprites refreshing their .texture each frame in sync() so real art swaps in; grey-box placeholders are acceptable for panel.party/icon.leader/icon.support.

STEP 5 — META-MECHANICS: STUB ONLY
Do NOT implement warrior_fire_all or rogue_apply_poison here. In the party-apply path, where a member has a non-null metaMechanic, leave a clear `// TODO(meta-mechanic): '<id>' not yet implemented — see party_system.txt / GDD` comment. No behavior change from meta-mechanics in this spec.

ACCEPTANCE (must be objectively verifiable):
1. Gate: `npm run -s typecheck` exits 0 AND the full test suite passes UNCHANGED (the no-party fallback must not perturb existing headless determinism). Report the commands and that they were green; explicitly confirm no pre-existing test was modified.
2. Determinism proof: grep src/sim for Math.random/Date.now/performance.now in the files you touched (characters.ts, state.ts, upgrades.ts) — zero new hits. Confirm partyPassives/partyWeaponPool/partyMembers are pure (no localStorage, no wall-clock) and are called only from the run-start/host path.
3. Pure-helper unit check (manual, via node/tsx or preview_eval on the built module): partyWeaponPool({leader:'rogue',supports:['warrior']}) returns the deduped union of rogue+warrior pools (e.g. ['knives','fireball','bomb-kunai','axe'] given the char_roster mapping) and partyPassives({leader:'warrior',supports:['explorer']}).damageMult === 1.15 and .hpMult === 1.15 (warrior weapon_mastery + explorer determination, trainingLevel 1). Report the observed values.
4. Run-start application: assemble a party {leader:'warrior', supports:['explorer']}, start a run, and read the live player via `window.__cc.raw()` (or getState): player.maxHp === round(300 * 1.15) with the explorer determination multiplier applied on top of warrior's 300 base (state the exact number you get and that hp===maxHp at start), and player.attackDamage reflects the warrior 1.15 damage multiplier. Report the numbers.
5. Draft reflects the party: with the above party set (partyWeaponPool includes 'axe','knives','fireball','bomb-kunai' but NOT, say, 'god-spread'), drive the sim to a level-up (`window.__cc` step loop) and inspect `raw().pendingUpgrades` across a few level-ups — every `weapon:new:<id>` candidate's id is a member of s.partyWeaponPool. Confirm at least one draft was inspected and no out-of-party new-weapon id appeared. Also confirm the no-party run (fresh state, partyWeaponPool empty) still draws from the full pool (fallback intact) and the gate tests pass.
6. Visual: character-select screen shows the party panel with a Leader badge and up to two Support slots (grey-box placeholders acceptable), assembling a party updates 'rs_party' in localStorage (verify with preview_eval), and starting with fewer than 3 shows the incomplete-party warning text (snapshot proof) while still allowing travel to the world map.
